1
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset floating
over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kick a pebble and let
it fly until it gets there.

3
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:29,340
Talking away by the gym's Kashiwa,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed that I was still
as full of energy as ever.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I somehow stir up my energy,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
Guts, there's a way.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
One nightmare,
and the streetscape that never changes

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
is gentler than ever.

9
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,700
the sun has already set.

11
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:53,900
Are there really yakitori stalls?

12
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointy hat,

13
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:02,420
from the waterworks on to the great measure.

14
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:04,080
The sunset falls.

15
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too, it'll end in a drop, won't it?

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,800
Magazine, maybe? Happiness again, they say.

17
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:14,660
Only after losing it did I realize.

18
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm such a fool.

19
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:27,660
Asking around until dusk, 3,000 people.

20
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:38,480
Take a look.

21
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:41,840
The stage for the Athens
Olympic battle is set.

22
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:45,460
All that's left is to wait
for the opening ceremony.

23
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:50,700
It's finally here, the Athens Olympics!

24
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:52,440
The opening ceremony is tomorrow, right?

25
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:55,020
It's the sports festival
held once every four years!

26
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:58,380
What's wrong, senpai?

27
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:03,060
Once every four years... now that you mention it,
there was something else too.

28
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:05,320
What happened four years ago?

29
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:08,420
Four years ago would be 2000, right?

30
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:11,040
That's right, the Y2K problem!

31
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:14,720
Yeah, the moment it turned to the year 2000.

32
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:19,400
But in the end,
nothing much happened, did it?

33
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:25,980
No, no, no, it's not that.
Something else important...

34
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:32,560
Wasn't it about four years ago that the phrase
"charisma clerk" became popular?

35
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:40,320
Oh yeah, the town was crawling with charisma clerks, wasn't it?
No, no, no, that's not what I meant!

36
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,780
Looks like someone's coming.

37
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,540
What's this? These documents?

38
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:58,520
Unsolved case files, right?

39
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:01,760
No, no, the Olympics are about to start.

40
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:04,120
Hasn't that guy woken up yet?

41
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:06,880
That guy? Which guy?

42
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:11,960
Oh right,
this year is the year Higurashi wakes up.

43
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:17,720
Let me explain about Higurashi
for first-time viewers.

44
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:20,060
His full name is Higurashi Neruō.

45
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:21,480
He's a police officer.

46
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:24,980
Officially,
he's assigned to the Kōen-mae police box.

47
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,620
He's always loved sleeping,

48
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:30,100
and before long,
his sleep kept getting longer and longer.

49
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:34,660
Now he only wakes up once every four years,
in Olympic years.

50
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:38,440
But in return,
Higurashi has incredible psychic powers,

51
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:42,980
and in the brief time he's awake,
he can solve numerous unsolved cases.

52
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:46,240
That's why he's kept his
job and hasn't been fired.

53
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:48,980
However,

54
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:57,840
If we accidentally wake Higurashi
in a year that isn't an Olympic year,

55
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:01,220
it'll be a disaster,
so we have to be careful.

56
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:05,000
When it comes to Olympic years,
it's Higurashi-san, isn't it?

57
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,580
Didn't he also want to watch Athens?

58
00:04:08,340 --> 00:04:10,000
What, he still hasn't shown up?

59
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,880
You can just wake him up
quickly and bring him here.

60
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:15,140
We have a mountain of
cases that need his powers.

61
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:16,940
Don't look at us, we can't do much about it.

62
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:20,540
Ryotsu, you go and bring him here.

63
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:24,400
No, if you go alone you'll slack off,
so go with Nakagawa.

64
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,800
Higurashi's room is, if I remember right,

65
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:29,800
Wake up, Higurashi!

66
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,460
W-what is it, Ryo-san?

67
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:39,460
Why are you here?

68
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:41,640
This is Higurashi's room, you know.

69
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:45,740
Ever since we rebuilt Ryo's place the other day,
it's been my room.

70
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:51,440
Come to think of it, when we rebuilt Ryo's place,
Higurashi didn't have a room, did he?

71
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:53,660
Then where is Higurashi-san now?

72
00:04:56,060 --> 00:04:57,500
That's right, over there!

73
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:06,720
Of all places, in the station's morgue,

74
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:09,840
the place where unidentified
bodies are kept, right?

75
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:12,480
What kind of place is he putting him in?

76
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:15,840
He said he wanted to sleep somewhere quiet.

77
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,600
This place is quiet, isn't it?

78
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:19,860
I suppose it is.

79
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:23,060
I think he's around here somewhere.

80
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:29,060
Found it.

81
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:31,660
Higurashi, wake up!

82
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:33,720
He's not here!

83
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,440
What's going on, Ryotsu?

84
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:39,320
I don't know either.

85
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:42,500
I'm in charge of the morgue, though.

86
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:44,700
Where was Higurashi?

87
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:45,940
Higurashi.

88
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:48,140
He was sleeping in the morgue, right?

89
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,780
He was in a locker in C3.

90
00:05:52,460 --> 00:05:54,560
A locker in C3?

91
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:55,940
That's right.

92
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,280
Well...

93
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:03,780
The bereaved family came by the day
before yesterday and took him away.

94
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:06,520
The bereaved family?

95
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:11,040
Yes, that was a Mr. Meguro
who lives in Saitama, right?

96
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:16,620
Hearing a rumor that the eldest son, who had
been out of contact for years, had died in Tokyo,

97
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:19,020
his family came looking for him.

98
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:21,460
His physical features matched as well,

99
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:26,220
and above all, there was a paper with
"Meguro" written on it taped to the locker.

100
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:28,820
You idiot, look properly!

101
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:30,960
Not that, it's fire!

102
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,640
You're right.

103
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:35,603
I hope you won't be too surprised, but

104
00:06:35,653 --> 00:06:38,480
the one who was there was
an officer from our station.

105
00:06:39,540 --> 00:06:42,840
Listen, stay calm. He's alive.

106
00:06:44,440 --> 00:07:07,680
!
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah

107
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:10,280
Dad, did you remember to
set the answering machine?

108
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,460
No good. Nobody's answering.

109
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:23,260
Maybe they're at the funeral.

110
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:25,340
A funeral!?

111
00:07:25,740 --> 00:07:29,340
Yes, I think so. I believe they
said the farewell ceremony is today.

112
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:31,940
Say the important things first!

113
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,700
S-sorry.

114
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:37,116
If you dawdle, Higurashi will be cremated!

115
00:07:37,166 --> 00:07:40,180
No, he may have already been cremated.

116
00:07:41,060 --> 00:07:44,520
Don't you have an emergency contact?
A cell phone or something?

117
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:47,780
Now that you mention it,
there's his younger brother's cell phone.

118
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:51,620
It's starting.

119
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:53,480
Who is it?

120
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:55,060
Turn it off.

121
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:00,220
It's no good. It won't go through.

122
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:01,540
What are we gonna do!

123
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:01,740
Ugh...

124
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:03,820
Yeah, yeah.

125
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:04,420
Over on your end.

126
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:06,300
The name is Higurashi.

127
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:07,980
No, it's Higurashi, not...

128
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:10,480
Higurashi.

129
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:11,640
Senpai.

130
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,300
What are you doing, Nakagawa?

131
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:17,340
This is a matter of whether
Higurashi gets cremated or not!

132
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:18,080
Here, this.

133
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,680
Higurashi Family Funeral Guide, this one.

134
00:08:22,060 --> 00:08:24,520
This is the house, no doubt about it.

135
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:27,880
It says the funeral hall on it.
Call them right away!

136
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:28,340
Yes.

137
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:28,887
Yes,

138
00:08:28,937 --> 00:08:32,520
If it's Mr. Megure's funeral,
then it's definitely ours.

139
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:33,680
I see.

140
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:35,740
Stop the funeral right away!

141
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:38,324
Even if you say to stop it,

142
00:08:38,374 --> 00:08:40,616
the service ended just a moment ago,

143
00:08:40,666 --> 00:08:44,380
and everyone has already
headed to the crematorium.

144
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,980
What! Cremation!

145
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,740
Nakagawa, let's go!

146
00:08:50,980 --> 00:08:51,380
Yes.

147
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:56,240
We have to stop them, no matter what!

148
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,980
Higurashi's going to be cremated!

149
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:01,300
The phone will be unavailable
for about 10 minutes,

150
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:04,400
so our fiber-optic line is
finally connected, right?

151
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,400
The arrangements for the
family's funeral are ready.

152
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,700
Damn it, why won't this thing connect?

153
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:11,800
Higurashi!

154
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:16,720
Let us say our final farewells.

155
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:21,200
Big brother,
you won't have to suffer anymore.

156
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:22,960
Rest in peace.

157
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:26,980
I think he just moved.

158
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:28,520
Stop that!

159
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:31,940
Ichiro won't be able to pass
on to the afterlife in peace.

160
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:34,240
No, thank you.

161
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:34,860
Yes.

162
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:42,820
I thought I just heard Ichiro's voice.

163
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:45,800
Big brother is saying goodbye to everyone.

164
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:54,180
Don't you dare burn him!

165
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:03,080
It's hot!

166
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,600
I told you,
it's a case of mistaken identity!

167
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:06,580
Dad, Mom!

168
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:10,800
Heichūrō!

169
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,960
Why?

170
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:15,880
The newspaper said my funeral was being held,
Translation>
so I came over in a panic.

171
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:17,300
so I came over in a panic.

172
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:20,460
Then who's being burned in there?

173
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:23,000
I keep telling you, it's a mix-up!

174
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:24,360
Phew!

175
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:27,100
Huh?

176
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:29,260
It's hissing, the hissing hurts!

177
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:32,100
Aaah!

178
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:33,480
Aaah!

179
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:35,240
Aaah!

180
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:36,460
No!

181
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:38,160
No!

182
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:40,420
Aaah!

183
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:43,780
No!

184
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:45,100
Aaah!

185
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:45,180
No!

186
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:46,180
No!

187
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:51,800
Higurashi!

188
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,560
Ryo-san!

189
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,920
Hey! Did you see that? Inside just now!

190
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:00,300
See what?

191
00:11:00,940 --> 00:11:03,520
Higurashi was right here, wasn't he!
Faintly!

192
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:06,700
I didn't see anything, though...

193
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:10,520
Was it my imagination?
Then where's that Higurashi guy?

194
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:13,340
That was Ryo-san just now, right!

195
00:11:42,420 --> 00:11:44,380
I wonder why I'm in a place like this.

196
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:45,580
Hey, part-timer!

197
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:47,660
That's not good, you know.

198
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:50,060
Wandering around outside
dressed like that...

199
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:55,720
What year is it now, A.D.?

200
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:58,160
Obviously it's 2004.

201
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:01,420
Four full years have passed.

202
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:09,700
I wonder what happened
to Morning Musume by now.

203
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:14,080
Maybe that new girl who joined before,
Gomaki, has become the leader.

204
00:12:16,660 --> 00:12:17,380
I can sense it.

205
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:20,060
This is definitely the smell of a crime.

206
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:25,980
The culprit is lying in wait
for prey in the haunted house.

207
00:12:26,540 --> 00:12:27,440
It's pitch-black.

208
00:12:28,140 --> 00:12:29,000
It's scary.

209
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:42,500
Give back the wallet
you just found out about.

210
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,180
Wow, it's the real thing!

211
00:12:46,180 --> 00:12:47,860
What's going on, Ryotsu?

212
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,400
Where is Higurashi?

213
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:51,880
I want to know that myself.

214
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:54,080
He was definitely in there, though.

215
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:57,080
There's no escape route
inside the furnace, either.

216
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:00,020
It's me.

217
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,540
Pickpocketed at the amusement park.

218
00:13:02,540 --> 00:13:05,360
Don't call me over every
little thing like that.

219
00:13:05,780 --> 00:13:07,700
I've got more pressing
things to deal with here.

220
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:09,420
Higurashi has disappeared.

221
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:13,420
What!? You're saying Higurashi was
the one who caught the pickpocket?!

222
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:17,920
Why is Higurashi, who was supposed to be at the crematorium,
in a haunted house?

223
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:20,080
It might be a case of mistaken identity.

224
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:22,640
I'm telling you, it's not scary.

225
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,520
It's child's play, isn't it?

226
00:13:29,520 --> 00:13:31,820
Ryo-san, Nakagawa, it's been a long time.

227
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:34,480
It suits you too well!

228
00:13:36,220 --> 00:13:38,580
Before I knew it,
I'd come to this amusement park.

229
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:41,240
You were at the crematorium, you know!

230
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:43,540
Everyone's waiting for you.

231
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:44,860
Let's head back to the station!

232
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:45,540
Yeah.

233
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:52,440
Hii...

234
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:54,620
What's wrong?

235
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:57,440
It's a haunted house, after all.

236
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:59,020
There are bound to be
some will-o'-the-wisps.

237
00:13:59,280 --> 00:13:59,880
Eeek!

238
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:00,900
Eeek!

239
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:01,720
Eeek!

240
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:02,460
Hey!

241
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:03,760
What's wrong, Higurashi!

242
00:14:04,340 --> 00:14:05,140
Eeek!

243
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:07,300
Eeek!

244
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:11,680
No! No!

245
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:19,460
That's right, Ryo-san!
The leader of the Monmono!

246
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:24,720
Did you see it, Nakagawa?

247
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:26,080
Y-yes...

248
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,720
Teleportation?

249
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:31,260
You! Of all the nonsense to come out with!

250
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:33,040
It's true, I tell you!

251
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:37,160
I saw it with my own eyes.
I still can't believe it!

252
00:14:38,540 --> 00:14:41,960
He can only stay awake for 24 hours!

253
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:44,320
We have to bring Higurashi
back as soon as possible.

254
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:47,040
Because this many
incidents are waiting for us.

255
00:14:50,820 --> 00:14:52,580
Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box.

256
00:14:53,880 --> 00:14:54,940
Higurashi-san?

257
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:55,720
What?

258
00:14:56,260 --> 00:14:57,580
Where are you right now?

259
00:14:58,420 --> 00:14:59,780
Mount Fuji?

260
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:03,460
I woke up here,

261
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:07,520
and there happened to be a poacher, so

262
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:08,860
I caught him.

263
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:13,080
Got it. I'll arrange it right away.

264
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:16,280
Can't you teleport back from there?

265
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:18,660
Teleport?

266
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:20,880
You haven't noticed it yourself?

267
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:24,000
You've acquired the power of teleportation!

268
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:25,440
No wonder.

269
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:28,780
But I don't know how to do it.

270
00:15:28,780 --> 00:15:29,620
I see.

271
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:31,320
That's the way it is.

272
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:33,500
You go pick him up quickly.

273
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:35,520
Understood.

274
00:15:42,940 --> 00:15:43,960
It's over there.

275
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:49,100
Thank you for your cooperation.

276
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:52,420
No, it's the least we could do.

277
00:15:52,940 --> 00:15:55,080
Well, we should be heading back too.

278
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:57,600
Everyone's been waiting
for you with bated breath.

279
00:15:58,100 --> 00:15:59,200
Hey, mister.

280
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:00,320
What is it?

281
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:03,160
Mind if I take a quick smoke break?

282
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:06,280
I get antsy when I run out of cigarettes.

283
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:09,820
Tch, you're hopeless. Just one, got it?

284
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:12,940
Heh. Thanks.

285
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:23,440
E-eek.

286
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:25,440
What's wrong? Higurashi-san?

287
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:27,540
Hin-ga, hin-ga.

288
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:28,340
Eek?

289
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:31,680
Hin-ga, hin-ga, hin-ga.

290
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:35,040
Come to think of it,
didn't he also look at the fire earlier?

291
00:16:37,280 --> 00:17:00,800


292
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,860
He teleports whenever he sees fire,
you know.

293
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:06,189
First the crematorium, then the
will-o'-the-wisp at the haunted house,

294
00:17:06,239 --> 00:17:07,840
and on top of that,
the flame from a lighter.

295
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:09,520
So that's how it was.

296
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:12,400
So where is Higurashi now?

297
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:18,100
Yes, Kōen-mae Police Box.

298
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:19,880
Where are you now?

299
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:22,000
Kagoshima?

300
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:25,280
Yeah, I can see Sakurajima clearly.

301
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,460
Apparently you can even
see it erupt sometimes.

302
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:29,820
Erupt?

303
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:32,000
Whoa!

304
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:34,140
It erupted! It's spewing fire!

305
00:17:34,460 --> 00:17:36,280
Fire! Fire!

306
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,960
Don't look at the fire! Higurashi!

307
00:17:40,380 --> 00:17:42,680
Higurashi! Hey! Higurashi!

308
00:17:43,100 --> 00:17:44,680
Higurashi! Answer me!

309
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:45,780
Higurashi!

310
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:50,020
He teleported again!

311
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:55,660
Yes! Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box!

312
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:57,860
It's Higurashi!

313
00:17:57,860 --> 00:17:59,000
Where are you?

314
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:01,900
Kagoshima?

315
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:04,640
Then bring him back here right away!

316
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:06,000
Don't say such unreasonable things!

317
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:09,380
Senpai, we'll get there in no
time if we take my Concorde!

318
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:12,120
Well then, shall we go?

319
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:18,020
We came all the way to Hawaii,
and we can't see a thing?

320
00:18:18,700 --> 00:18:23,040
It can't be helped. You teleport somewhere whenever you see fire,
after all.

321
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:28,280
You can take that off now.

322
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:32,080
Ryo-san, this is...

323
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:34,380
It's the file on an unsolved case.

324
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:36,440
Looking at it here?

325
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:38,680
Let me relax a little longer.

326
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:41,820
You can only stay awake for 24 hours.

327
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:43,660
Half of it's already gone.

328
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:45,840
We don't have time to dawdle.

329
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:47,960
Fine, I get it.

330
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:55,240
I see it, I can see it!

331
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:57,720
The culprit in the 200 million yen robbery?

332
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:59,160
Where is he?

333
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,540
I can see a river.

334
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:02,960
The Arakawa

335
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:05,160
Right on the money, Kita-Senju.

336
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:05,980
Here it is.

337
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:08,920
Right, contact Japan immediately.

338
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:10,500
Alright, got it.

339
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:14,880
You're under arrest on suspicion
of the 200 million yen robbery.

340
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:18,840
How did you figure out where he was?

341
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:21,820
This guy's currently on the bullet train.

342
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:24,300
He'll be arriving at Tokyo Station soon.

343
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:29,700
He's not moving.

344
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:33,220
This guy's disguised himself with a mustache,
a beard, and glasses.

345
00:19:33,220 --> 00:19:34,620
He's working part-time under a false name.

346
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:37,260
It's a convenience store near his home.

347
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:41,240
The culprit in this case is...

348
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,660
Actually,
he's the eldest son of the family next door.

349
00:19:51,420 --> 00:19:54,360
Higurashi, you came back after all.

350
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,440
Hello, it's been a long time.

351
00:19:57,740 --> 00:19:59,980
Just a little more, and I'm counting on you.

352
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:03,500
There's still more? I'm hungry.

353
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:05,400
What kind of nonsense are you talking about?

354
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:08,600
You can only stay awake for 24 hours,
you know.

355
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:10,900
Shouldn't we let him rest a little?

356
00:20:11,420 --> 00:20:11,820
Yes, you're right.

357
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:14,780
Nakagawa, go buy him something.

358
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:15,360
Yes.

359
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:19,560
Shall we take a smoke break too?

360
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:22,220
Nakagawa, what are you doing?

361
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,540
What are you talking about, a cigarette?

362
00:20:24,540 --> 00:20:25,960
Did you forget?

363
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:29,180
Higurashi teleports whenever he sees fire,
you know.

364
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:30,820
That's right.

365
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,220
I'm thirsty.

366
00:20:33,660 --> 00:20:35,900
Reiko, make us some tea.

367
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:36,420
Yes.

368
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:38,120
Wait a moment.

369
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:44,600
What's wrong, Ryotsu? From this room,
I can see the gas stove's flame!

370
00:20:45,060 --> 00:20:50,400
I see. Sorry,
but could you go buy some drinks outside?

371
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:51,240
Yes.

372
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:56,920
I'm just going to go out back for a smoke.
No, wait.

373
00:20:56,920 --> 00:21:03,300
Excuse me, I'd like to ask for directions.

374
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:04,580
I'll go.

375
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:08,280
The Athens Olympics start today.

376
00:21:09,040 --> 00:21:11,860
The opening ceremony should
be starting about now.

377
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:17,840
Speaking of which, I asked you to record four years' worth of
"Warate Ii Tomo no Telephone Shocking," didn't I?

378
00:21:18,380 --> 00:21:20,620
And I even paid you in advance for the job.

379
00:21:21,100 --> 00:21:23,220
Damn, I completely forgot.

380
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:27,460
I'll let you watch it at your
leisure once work is done.

381
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:30,140
Just going to the bathroom.

382
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:36,020
I need to find someone who's recorded it.

383
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:40,260
Well, look at that,
the opening ceremony is on right now!

384
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:50,300
What's wrong, Higurashi?

385
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:53,400
Fire! Fire! Fire!

386
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:57,920
And now the Olympic
cauldron is about to be lit.

387
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:59,200
Aaaaah!

388
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:03,940
Aaaaah!

389
00:22:07,380 --> 00:22:18,480
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

390
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:21,120
I loved the Olympics more
than three square meals a day.

391
00:22:25,260 --> 00:22:33,300
No word from Higurashi. It's been almost 24 hours.
There's something I'm a little worried about.

392
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:44,980
Well, Higurashi's teleporting... First it was a nearby amusement park, then Mount Fuji, then Kagoshima, then Hawaii.
It's getting farther and farther away.

393
00:22:44,980 --> 00:22:53,140
Aaaaah! We interrupt the Olympic
broadcast with shocking news from America.

394
00:22:53,840 --> 00:23:00,740
Incredibly, intelligent life has reportedly been discovered on Mars.
This is footage from the Mars rover.

395
00:23:01,860 --> 00:23:08,100
This is... Higurashi? Why is he on Mars?
Can humans even live on Mars?

396
00:23:08,780 --> 00:23:11,120
Maybe he's awakened to a new power again.

397
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:17,580
He seems to be writing something
like letters in the ground.

398
00:23:21,180 --> 00:23:25,560
I'm sleepy, so I'm going to sleep here.

399
00:23:31,180 --> 00:23:33,440
Come wake me up in four years.

400
00:23:37,540 --> 00:23:39,980
How are we supposed to come wake you up?

401
00:24:20,460 --> 00:24:22,280
So what if we're poor?

402
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:23,280
That's not it.

403
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:26,640
I'll do things my way, just as I please.

404
00:24:26,640 --> 00:24:28,040
That's all there is to it.

405
00:24:28,040 --> 00:24:28,780
Amazing!

406
00:24:28,780 --> 00:24:30,820
The Chief's thunderbolt of a scolding

407
00:24:30,820 --> 00:24:32,620
Smoke coming out of my head

408
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:35,660
If I run away, the camera will catch me.

409
00:24:35,660 --> 00:24:37,360
Well, that's something to celebrate.

410
00:24:37,360 --> 00:24:39,840
In the flower of Edo,

411
00:24:39,840 --> 00:24:42,040
The Liangshan horde

412
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:42,860
Thanks as always.

413
00:24:42,860 --> 00:24:45,420
Raging wildly

414
00:24:45,420 --> 00:24:47,580
Lazybones 9×2

415
00:24:47,580 --> 00:24:48,980
Ten games, ten games

416
00:24:50,460 --> 00:24:56,380
Sasuiko, suiko, matsu, gunko, matsu, gunrai, matsu, gun,
where you sleep, where you live.

417
00:24:56,980 --> 00:25:00,260
Yabura-kōji, bura-kōji, paipo paipo paipo no

418
00:25:00,260 --> 00:25:04,300
Shūringan shūringan no,
kūrin raifu, kūrin rarii no

419
00:25:04,300 --> 00:25:08,480
Poppo kokkii no, poppo konaa no,
chō kyūmei no Chōsukein

420
00:25:16,100 --> 00:25:20,060
What? Terai's going camping
to show off to the kids?

421
00:25:20,460 --> 00:25:23,080
Are you sure about this?
Underestimate nature and you'll regret it.

422
00:25:23,080 --> 00:25:26,400
Well, I suppose I'll lend a hand this once.

423
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:28,100
Terai, good luck!

424
00:25:28,100 --> 00:25:30,920
Next time: Papa, the young camp boss!

425
00:25:30,920 --> 00:25:31,940
Take care, okay?

426
00:25:33,660 --> 00:25:36,420
Over there is Kame-ari.

427
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:39,600
Well, surely Kame-ari.

428
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:44,240
Everybody come on over to our town!

429
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:45,800
Thank you.

